AMDMIGraphX (release/rocm-rel-6.4, pinned commit 7466a4cd2fa39ae2d0f89f747262cd962a22cfc4):
two correctness/compatibility fixes to src/onnx/parse_resize.cpp, discovered
while getting AudioMuse-AI's CLAP audio encoder to compile under
MIGraphXExecutionProvider on gfx803. Both are backports of fixes already
merged to upstream `develop` but never cherry-picked onto this release
branch.

--- Fix 1: accept keep_aspect_ratio_policy="stretch" -------------------------

Why: MIGraphX's Resize parser unconditionally throws
"PARSE_Resize: keep_aspect_ratio_policy is not supported!" the moment that
attribute is present on a node at all - regardless of its value. ONNX
Runtime's own graph loader materializes schema-declared default attribute
values for every node during Graph::Resolve() (confirmed by dumping ORT's
post-transform graph: a Resize node with the attribute stripped from the
source .onnx file came back with keep_aspect_ratio_policy="stretch" anyway,
which is opset-18's spec default), so any Resize node built by a
reasonably-recent exporter trips this, even though "stretch" changes nothing
about the op's actual semantics (it is the default, no-op policy).

What: only throw when the policy is present AND not "stretch". Exact upstream
fix: github.com/ROCm/AMDMIGraphX PR #4875, "Accept keep_aspect_ratio_policy=
stretch in Resize parser" (merged to develop 2026-05-13, never backported to
release/rocm-rel-6.4).

--- Fix 2: use standard strides when computing gather indices ----------------

Why: this branch's linear-mode lowering (a from-scratch, pre-native-kernel
implementation carried on this release branch - upstream `develop` has since
replaced the whole approach with a JIT-backed resize op, PR #4553, too large
a change to backport here) unrolls bilinear interpolation into reshape +
gather + slice/sub/mul/add at parse time. calc_neighbor_points() converts a
multi-dimensional neighbor index into a flat buffer offset via
`in_s.index(...)`, which assumes in_s has standard (contiguous, row-major)
strides. in_s is whatever shape the Resize node's input instruction actually
carries at that point in the graph, which is not guaranteed to be standard
once earlier graph-optimizer passes (e.g. a Transpose folded into a
non-default-stride view) have run on it - producing a silently wrong flat
offset with no error of any kind.

What: call `.as_standard()` before computing indices, forcing a
canonical-strides view. Exact upstream fix: github.com/ROCm/AMDMIGraphX PR
#4444, "Fix bug in parse_resize with nonstandard input shapes" (merged to
develop 2025-12-12, commit bb32124, never backported to release/rocm-rel-6.4).

--- What this patch does NOT fix ---------------------------------------------

These two fixes make MIGraphX successfully parse and run CLAP's audio
encoder (previously: hard parse failure). They do NOT make the output
correct: isolated Resize-only tests (both single-axis and CLAP's real
128x1001->256x256 two-axis geometry) confirm the Resize computation itself
is correct post-patch (cosine similarity 1.0 against a numpy reference and
against onnxruntime's CPU EP). But comparing MIGraphX's own "ref" (CPU,
no GPU codegen/fusion) target against its "gpu" target - same parsed
program, same IR, only the target-specific compile pass differs - showed a
cosine similarity of ~0.075 between them: the actual remaining divergence is
in MIGraphX's GPU-target codegen/fusion for this network, not the ONNX
parser. That is a substantially deeper issue (comparable in kind to the
MIOpen GPU-codegen correctness bugs already documented for this arch in the
AudioMuse-AI ROCm plugin's docs/ARCH_NOTES.md) and is not addressed here.
Applying this patch alone is not sufficient to make MIGraphXExecutionProvider
safe to use for CLAP on gfx803 - see that plugin's docs for the current
recommended path (ROCMExecutionProvider with ConvActivationFusion disabled).

Applies to: AMDMIGraphX @ release/rocm-rel-6.4, gfx803 only (this Dockerfile
is gfx803-exclusive; other arches build from upstream's develop branch,
which already has both fixes).

